<title>MEXICO: Tribasa seeks $1 bln in Chilean projects.</title>
<headline>Tribasa seeks $1 bln in Chilean projects.</headline>
<dateline>CANCUN, Mexico 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican construction firm Tribasa aims to raise its share of Chilean highway concessions to $1 billion, the firm's director general said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;To reach construction contracts of $1 billion -- we already have $700 million -- that's Tribasa's target,&quot; Director General Alfredo Magni said at a business owners conference in the Caribbean resort of Cancun.</p>
<p>Magni said the Chilean government plans to offer highway concessions totaling $4 billion by the year 2000.</p>
<p>Magni added that Tribasa also hoped to achieve a total capacity of $300 million per year in production and sales.</p>
<p>((--Veronica Galan, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7907))</p>
